(25727, 'Agro-Ecological Land Resources Assessment for Agricultural Development Planning (World Soil ...', 'by Unknown Author', '', '', '1991', 'Food &amp; Agriculture Organization of the United Nations', '0', 0, '9789251033890', '', 'C008', 'Agro-Ecological Land Resources Assessment for Agricultural Development Planning (World Soil Resources Reports), was published 1991 under ISBN 9789251033890 and ISBN 9251033897.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:17:21', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(25736, 'Deformation of Soils, Vol. 1', 'Associazione Geotecnica Italiana Staff', '', '', '1991', 'Ashgate Publishing Company', '0', 0, '9789054100027', '', 'C008', 'Associazione Geotecnica Italiana Staff is the author of \\\'Deformation of Soils, Vol. 1\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9789054100027 and ISBN 9054100028.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:17:21', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(25770, 'World Food Problem', 'Grigg, David B.', '', '', '1993', 'Wiley &amp; Sons, Incorporated, John', '0', 0, '9780631176336', '', 'C008', 'In The World Food Problem, updated in every respect since its first edition in 1985, David Grigg provides a full account of who is hungry, where and why. The causes of hunger are manifold and complex: population growth, environmental degradation, poverty, inefficient farming, poor distribution, inappropriate aid, war, drought, famine, corruption, and incompetence are among them. The great strength and value of this outstanding book lie at once in the author\\\'s understanding of the nature and scope of the problem, and in his clear analysis of the factors operating in a wide range of instances. The search for simple solutions is not only pointless but, he shows only too vividly, their implementation is frequently damaging and counterproductive.Grigg, David B. is the author of \\\'World Food Problem\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780631176336 and ISBN 0631176330.', '0.000000', 0.00, 53.59, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:17:21', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
