(28063, 'Machinery Maintenance', 'Deere and Company Staff', '', '', '1991', 'Deere &amp; Company, John Deere Publishing', '0', 0, '9780866911306', '', 'C008', 'A basic introduction to farm machinery & its care. MACHINERY MAINTENANCE is for readers without prior machinery experience. It is different from Deere & Company\\\'s FMO Preventive Maintenance which is for those with some machinery knowledge. MACHINERY MAINTENANCE is for different readers. The technical material is presented in a manner more suitable to nontechnical readers: People without any machinery experience, those who speak English as a second language, & readers in the third world countries. CONTENTS: How Engines Develop Power, Intake & Exhaust Systems, Fuel Systems, Oil Systems, Cooling Systems, Electrical Systems, Power Trains, Hydraulics & More.Deere and Company Staff is the author of \\\'Machinery Maintenance\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780866911306 and ISBN 0866911308.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:17:36', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(28083, 'Fruit Berry and Nut Inventory', 'Whealy, Kent', '', '', '1993', 'Seed Savers Exchange, Incorporated', '0', 0, '9780961397753', '', 'C008', '\\\"This 500-page directory lists all the fruit, berry, nut and edible tropicals available by mail order in the United States. Each variety is cross-referenced according to its source...If you are looking for dwarf fruit trees for the patio or lime berries for the greenhouse, this book will tell you how to find them.\\\"Whealy, Kent is the author of \\\'Fruit Berry and Nut Inventory\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780961397753 and ISBN 0961397756.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:17:36', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(28121, 'Women Wielding the Hoe Lessons from Rural Africa for Feminist Theory and Development Practice', 'Bryceson, Deborah, Ardener, Shirley, Waldren, Jackie', '', '', '1995', 'Berg Publishers', '0', 0, '9781859730683', '', 'C008', 'How effective is western aid-agency intervention in Africa? What can African women do to manage the AIDS crisis? Can western feminist theory be applied to the rural African context? These vital issues, and many others, are considered in this topical book by eminent scholars and development consultants. The book aims to increase awareness of the importance of women agricultural producers to African material development and to expose the western biases that have traditionally pervaded the study of rural African women. The authors\\\' critical analyses of conventional research methodology and key \\\'women and development\\\' debates over the last three decades will stimulate new research perspectives. Students and scholars of development, development workers and policymakers will all find this book fascinating reading.Bryceson, Deborah is the author of \\\'Women Wielding the Hoe Lessons from Rural Africa for Feminist Theory and Development Practice\\\', published 1995 under ISBN 9781859730683 and ISBN 185973068X.', '0.000000', 0.00, 155.50, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:17:36', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
