(28984, 'Introduction to Agricultural Geography', 'Grigg, David B.', '', '', '1995', 'Routledge', '0', 0, '9780415084420', '', 'C008', 'Throughout the world, agriculture is by far the most important economic activity, with a wide range of factors influencing the huge variety of farming methods. An Introduction to Agricultural Geography defines not only the causes of such diversity but also provides the essential reasons for its study. Contrasting the farming structures and techniques for both developed and developing nations, the author highlights the growing economic and environmental impact of agriculture in the face of increasing social and cultural demands.Grigg, David B. is the author of \\\'Introduction to Agricultural Geography\\\', published 1995 under ISBN 9780415084420 and ISBN 0415084423.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:17:40', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
