(35031, 'Farm Workshop and Maintenance', 'Moore, V.', '', '', '1992', 'Wiley &amp; Sons, Incorporated, John', '0', 0, '9780632025381', '', 'C008', 'Few farmers can afford a resident full-time mechanic, but when farm machinery breaks down it must be back in action without delay. The ability to get on with sowing or harvesting, for instance, can mean the difference between profit and loss on a particular crop. This thoroughly practical book, based on a successful series of \\\"Workshop\\\" articles in FARMERS WEEKLY, explains service and maintenance problems and workshop skills. Each job is illustrated with diagrams and/or photographs which describe the correct method of work and the permissible short cuts. FARMERS WEEKLY is Britain\\\'s leading farming journal. A deep practical knowledge of everyday farming, provided by the six farms it owns or manages is expressed in its unrivalled coverage of the farming scene.Moore, V. is the author of \\\'Farm Workshop and Maintenance\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780632025381 and ISBN 0632025387.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:09', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(35036, 'Diseases of Sheep', 'Martin, W., Aitken, I.', '', '', '1991', 'Wiley &amp; Sons, Incorporated, John', '0', 0, '9780632029570', '', 'C008', 'Nearly 50 specialists, many of whom are from the Animal Diseases Research Association, have contributed to the new edition of this study of the major diseases of sheep. Completely revised, updated, rearranged, and expanded to take into account developments in the seven years since the last edition.The coverage of diseases and conditions has been extended and there are new sections on common surgical procedures and zoonotic infections linked to sheep. Also included, is a new section on the perinatal period.Martin, W. is the author of \\\'Diseases of Sheep\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780632029570 and ISBN 0632029579.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:09', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(35045, 'Goat', 'Standing Committee on Agriculture Staff', '', '', '1991', 'CSIRO Publishing', '0', 0, '9780643051201', '', 'C008', 'These Model Codes of Practice are intended as a guide for people responsible for the welfare and husbandry of a range of animals. The Codes are kept under review to take account of advances in the understanding of animal physiology and behavioural technology, changes in animal husbandry and their relationships to the welfare of animals.Standing Committee on Agriculture Staff is the author of \\\'Goat\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780643051201 and ISBN 0643051201.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:09', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(35046, 'Feral Livestock Animals : Destruction or Capture, Handling and Marketing', 'Agricultural Council, Australian, Scarm Staff', '', '', '1992', 'CSIRO Publishing', '0', 0, '9780643051225', '', 'C008', 'These Model Codes of Practice are intended as a guide for people responsible for the welfare and husbandry of a range of animals. The Codes are kept under review to take account of advances in the understanding of animal physiology and behavioural technology, changes in animal husbandry and their relationships to the welfare of animals.Agricultural Council, Australian is the author of \\\'Feral Livestock Animals : Destruction or Capture, Handling and Marketing\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780643051225 and ISBN 0643051228.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:09', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
