(35893, 'Hay and Forage Harvesting', 'Deere and Company Staff', '', '', '1993', 'Deere &amp; Company, John Deere Publishing', '0', 0, '9780866910460', '', 'C008', 'Discusses purposes & uses of different types of hay & forage equipment. Gives theory of operation for each type of machine using color illustrations. Covers all types - mowers, conditioners, rakes, balers, handling systems, cubers, choppers, blowers, & forage harvesters. Explains new large-package hay-handling systems. Explains proper operation & field adjustments. Shows correct steps in maintenance, storage & troubleshooting. CONTENTS: Harvesting methods, planning of harvest, mowers & conditioners, windrowers, rakes, balers, bale wagons, large rollbalers, loose hay stack wagons, hay cubers, choppers, forage harvesters, forage wagons, forage blowers, field operation & adjustments, selection of equipment, comparing harvesting systems, management of total systems & glossary & tables.Deere and Company Staff is the author of \\\'Hay and Forage Harvesting\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780866910460 and ISBN 0866910468.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:13', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
