(41274, 'Toward Sustainability A Plan for Collaborative Research on Agriculture and Natural Resource ...', 'Board on Agriculture Staff, National Research Council Staff', '', '', '1991', 'National Academies Press', '0', 0, '9780309045407', '', 'C008', 'Toward Sustainabilityrecommends a design for a new Collaborative Research Support Program (CRSP) for the U.S. Agency for International Development (AID). Currently, eight CRSPs operate under legislation that supports long-term agricultural research of benefit to developing countries and the United States. This book defines a process by which knowledge from all relevant AID-supported programs could be integrated and applied to advance profitable farming systems that improve local conditions and contribute to environmental goals. It makes recommendations on the types of competitive grants that should be made available under a new program, institutional participation, content of research proposals, and administrative procedures.Board on Agriculture Staff, National Research Council Staff is the author of \\\'Toward Sustainability A Plan for Collaborative Research on Agriculture and Natural Resource Management\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780309045407 and ISBN 0309045401.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:40', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(41275, 'Touch Wood Bc Forests at the Crossroads', 'Nixon, Bob, Travers, Ray, Drushka, Ken', '', '', '1993', 'Harbour Publishing Company, Limited', '0', 0, '9781550170740', '', 'C008', 'Ken Drushka worked as a journalist before spending sixteen years as a logger, silvicultural contractor and the operator of a custom sawmill. His work has been published in numerous periodicals, including Equity, Business in Vancouver, BC Report and Truck Logger. Drushka\\\'s books include the BC bestsellers Working in the Woods and Stumped: The Forest Industry in Transistion, Against Wind and Weather, Tie Hackers to Timber Harvesters and HR: A Biography of H.R. MacMillan, which won the 1996 Roderick Haig-Brown Regional BC Book Prize. He was also co-author of Three Men and a Forester (with Ian Mahood). Drushka passed away at the age of 63 in 2004.Nixon, Bob is the author of \\\'Touch Wood Bc Forests at the Crossroads\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9781550170740 and ISBN 1550170740.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:40', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(41289, 'Tractors and How They Work', 'Williams, Michael', '', '', '1992', 'Farming Press Limited', '0', 0, '9780852362396', '', 'C008', 'Williams, Michael is the author of \\\'Tractors and How They Work\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780852362396 and ISBN 0852362390.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:40', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(41295, 'Travels of an Olive Eater from Pit to Pit Plus How to Cure an Olive', 'Ryder, Virginia P.', '', '', '1991', 'Amigo Press', '0', 0, '9780935098037', '', 'C008', 'Travels of an Olive Eater from Pit to Pit is for the armchair traveler who loves adventure, good food & olives!...New friendships & funny situations just seem to happen when traveling alone & the author recalls her most interesting experiences. Black & white sketches give a delightful view of the countryside. Easy recipes & culinary secrets add a regional flavor. After reading Mrs. Ryder\\\'s book, you\\\'ll want to head for the south of Europe & leisurely follow the trail from pit to pit. How to Cure an Olive describes the many ways olives are cured, preserved & flavored. The same elements from nature as used by the ancient peoples are in these recipes: wind, water (sea), salt, ashes (lye). Detailed recipes duplicate the flavor & types of Mediterranean olives & are easy for anyone who wants to put up a small crock or two. If you have an olive tree nearby, you are in luck, if not it is fascinating to read how each type of olive is prepared. Imagine being able to cure your own olives!Ryder, Virginia P. is the author of \\\'Travels of an Olive Eater from Pit to Pit Plus How to Cure an Olive\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780935098037 and ISBN 0935098038.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:40', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(41297, 'Transforming Southern African Agriculture', 'Seidman, Ann Willcox', '', '', '1992', 'Africa World Press', '0', 0, '9780865431324', '', 'C008', 'Seidman, Ann Willcox is the author of \\\'Transforming Southern African Agriculture\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780865431324 and ISBN 0865431329.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:18:40', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
