(44635, 'Small Gas Engine Repair', 'Dempsey, Paul', '', '', '1993', 'McGraw-Hill', '0', 0, '9780830641420', '', 'C018', 'Save on repair costs with this do-it-yourselfer\\\'s guide! Here\\\'s all the hands-on guidance you need to troubleshoot and repair virtually any type of small gas engine used in lawn and garden equipment, chain saws, generators, and motor bikes. Whether your engine was made by Briggs & Stratton, Tecumseh, Eaton, Fairbanks-Morse, or any other manufacturer,Small Gas Engine Repair, 2Ecan show you how to fix it yourself with just a few simple tools. This practical handbook has been completely updated to include new American and foreign engines, carburetor rebuilding techniques, and new starter and ignition systems. You\\\'ll also find coverage of: Electrical systems Carburetor and fuel systems Cyclinder heads, valves, and piston rings Connecting rods, crankshafts, camshafts, bearing, and sealsDempsey, Paul is the author of \\\'Small Gas Engine Repair\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780830641420 and ISBN 0830641424.', '0.000000', 0.00, 78.24, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:21:30', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(44696, 'Automobile Design: Twelve Great Designers and Their Work', 'Barker, Ronald, Harding, Anthony', '', '', '1992', 'Society of Automotive Engineers, Incorporated', '0', 0, '9781560912101', '', 'C018', 'This book takes an in-depth look at the lives, personalities & technical achievements of twelve preeminent engineers who made significant & lasting contributions to the design & development of the automobile over the last century. From early pioneers to more recent innovators, AUTOMOBILE DESIGN features chapters on The Bolles, Frederick Lanchester, Henry M. Leland, Hans Ledwinka, Mark Birkigt, Ferdinand Porsche, Harry Miller, Vittorio Jano, Gabriel Voisin, Alec Issigonis, Dante Giacosa, & Colin Chapman.Barker, Ronald is the author of \\\'Automobile Design: Twelve Great Designers and Their Work\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9781560912101 and ISBN 1560912103.', '0.000000', 0.00, 106.28, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:21:30', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(44698, 'Performance Handling: How to Make Your Car Handle, Techniques for the 1990s', 'Alexander, Don', '', '', '1991', 'MBI Publishing Company LLC', '0', 0, '9780879384180', '', 'C018', 'Performance Handling By Don Alexander. Subtitled: How To Make Your Car Handle, Techniques For the 1990s. A complete look at handling for the highway, autocross course, and race track. This book thoroughly examines handling principles, suspension components and their effect on handling and ride modifications the match your driving style, and choosing the correct components for your car. Sftbd., 8 1/4\\\"x 10 3/4\\\", 160 pgs., 188 b&w photos,62 diagrams.Alexander, Don is the author of \\\'Performance Handling: How to Make Your Car Handle, Techniques for the 1990s\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780879384180 and ISBN 0879384182.', '0.000000', 0.00, 99.12, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:21:30', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(44699, 'How to Build Chevrolet Small-Block V-8 Race Engines, Vol. 8', 'Tarrant, Bill, Hawkinson, Chris', '', '', '1994', 'MBI Publishing Company LLC', '0', 0, '9780879387839', '', 'C018', 'How to Build Chevrolet Small-Block V-8 Race Engines Bill Tarrant & Chris Hawkinson. Proven, affordable, high-performance tips and techniques. Details on every step from selecting to testing the Chevy small-block V-8. Using a 35 and a 4 as demo engines, the authors discuss and illustrate inspections, tearing down an engine, machine work, porting and cylinder head work - all the way through break-in and tuning your race-ready engine. You can use stock parts instead of expensive aftermarket components and get great results! Sftbd., 8 1/4\\\"x 1 5/8\\\", 128 pgs., 151 b&w ill.Tarrant, Bill is the author of \\\'How to Build Chevrolet Small-Block V-8 Race Engines, Vol. 8\\\', published 1994 under ISBN 9780879387839 and ISBN 0879387831.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-18 23:21:30', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
