(49946, 'Setting Arteries in the Holy Land', 'Etkes, Adina N.', '', '', '1996', 'Donsun Publishing', '0', 0, '9780964120082', '', 'C031; C073', 'This book is an account of major engineering projects carried out by Perry W. Etkes, chief engineer, Northern Palestine, during the British Mandate of the Holy Land. Etkes built the Haifa Jaffa-Tel Aviv road; the Haifa-Acre road; the largest, most beautiful bridge in the country, near Haifa; the ship depot at Haifa port, amongst many other engineering feats that were vital to the development of the country. These achievements are documented by high quality black & white photographs, maps, correspondences, newspaper & magazine clippings. The book also reflects on the times & lifestyles of that era: the aspects of the British Regime, the bloody riots that divided the country, & anecdotes about individuals who left an imprint on the scene. For information write to: Donsun Publishing, P.O. Box 251584, Los Angeles, CA 90025; or call 213-876-7196.Etkes, Adina N. is the author of \\\'Setting Arteries in the Holy Land\\\', published 1996 under ISBN 9780964120082 and ISBN 0964120089.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:11:06', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
