(52942, 'Concrete Structures Euro-Design Handbook 94/95', 'Eibl, Josef', '', '', '1995', 'Wiley &amp; Sons, Incorporated, John', '0', 0, '9783433014295', '', 'C031; C073', 'Since the creation of the European Economic Community, concrete construction products and components can be freely exchanged among various users and countries. This development calls for the design and construction of civil engineering works and components that comply with uniform European regulations. Ernst & Sohn meets this need by publishing an English edition of the Beton-Kalender, one of the best-known standard works for civil engineers. Published annually since 1905, the Beton-Kalender contains proven know-how, which is now accessible to the entire European profession. This Handbook presents essential European Standards, practical examples for their application, and detailed accounts of the most recent developments in the field. Highlights from the table of contents: Hilsdorf, Concrete König, Kersken-Bradley, Actions on Structures Litzner, Design of Concrete Structures to ENV 1992 - Eurocode 2 Grasser, Kupfer, Pratsch, Feix, Design of Reinforced and Prestressed Concrete Elements for Bending with Axial Forces, Shear and Torsion Quast, Dimensioning of Slender Elements Related to Ultimate Limit States Influenced by Structura Deformations - Stability check Wölfel, European Codes and StandardsEibl, Josef is the author of \\\'Concrete Structures Euro-Design Handbook 94/95\\\', published 1995 under ISBN 9783433014295 and ISBN 3433014299.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:11:24', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
