(53838, 'Soil-Steel Bridges: Design and Construction', 'Abdel-Sayed, George, Bakht, Baidar, Jaeger, Leslie G.', '', '', '1994', 'McGraw-Hill Professional Publishing', '0', 0, '9780070030213', '', 'C031; C073', 'Tens of thousands of soil-steel bridges can be found in North America alone. Unfortunately, many of these short spans are in serious distress-largely because of lack of reliable design & construction data. This practical guide contains the technical information that will enable engineers to design & construct safe, economical soil-steel bridges; avoid the pitfalls-including metal corrosion-that lead to distress & failure; & restore bridges that are in disrepair. The book includes complete coverage of U.S. & Canadian design codes, as well as such neglected topics as the mechanics of soil-steel bridges; their special design features; the engineering properties of soil relevant to bridge design & construction; & the design of bridges that serve as conduits for water.Abdel-Sayed, George is the author of \\\'Soil-Steel Bridges: Design and Construction\\\', published 1994 under ISBN 9780070030213 and ISBN 0070030219.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:11:29', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
