(56941, 'Strength of Dilating Soil and Load-Holding Capacity of Deep Foundations: Introduction to The...', 'Sobolevsky, D. Yu', '', '', '1995', 'Taylor &amp; Francis Group', '0', 0, '9789054101642', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Introduces the theory and practical application of dilating soil and the load-holding capacity of deep foundations. Topics covered include dilatancy as a fundamental property of granular media, direct shear in conditions of constrained dilatancy, and load-holding capacity of a single pile.Sobolevsky, D. Yu is the author of \\\'Strength of Dilating Soil and Load-Holding Capacity of Deep Foundations: Introduction to Theory and Practical Application\\\', published 1995 under ISBN 9789054101642 and ISBN 9054101644.', '0.000000', 0.00, 255.15, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:52', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(56981, 'Building Conservation Contracts and Grant Aid A Practical Guide', 'Davey, Ken', '', '', '1992', 'Routledge', '0', 0, '9780419171409', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Davey, Ken is the author of \\\'Building Conservation Contracts and Grant Aid A Practical Guide\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780419171409 and ISBN 0419171401.', '0.000000', 0.00, 146.44, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:52', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(57004, 'Understanding House Construction', 'Kilpatrick, John A., O&#39;Connor, Rosanne', '', '', '1993', 'BuilderBooks', '0', 0, '9780867183825', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Learn how homes are built - from groundbreaking to final inspection - with this award-winning, easy-to-read book. A perfect introduction to the methods, materials & terms used in homebuilding, produced under the authority of the National Association of Home Builders. Each step of the construction process is presented in layman language with detailed explanations, photos & diagrams. Over eighty terms & materials are defined in the comprehensive glossary. Awards for this book include the Society of Technical Communication (STC) Distinguished Technical Communication Award in the United States & the Award of Excellence in STC\\\'s 1994 International Technical Publications competition. Judges\\\' comments included: \\\"Truly a superb introduction - I wish I\\\'d seen it before I bought my first house,\\\" & \\\"The language is exceptionally straightforward. This is a valuable resource...it covers everything.\\\" An essential reference for home buyers, real estate professionals, designers, public officials & anyone involved in the building trades. Other related titles include: LAND BUYING CHECKLIST, which offers help for the all-important land selection & purchase; ENERGY SMART BUILDING, for increasing the energy efficiency of homes; HOW TO HIRE & SUPERVISE SUBCONTRACTORS, invaluable information for anyone managing the construction process: & PRODUCTION CHECKLIST, a comprehensive \\\"to-do\\\" list for every phase of home construction. Ordering information: Home Builder Press of the National Association of Home Builders, 1201 15th St. NW, Washington, DC 20005. 800-223-2665 or 202-822-0643. Call for free catalog of home building books.Kilpatrick, John A. is the author of \\\'Understanding House Construction\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780867183825 and ISBN 0867183829.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:53', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(57017, 'Structure and Fate of Subducting Slabs', 'Lay, Thorne', '', '', '1996', 'Elsevier Science &amp; Technology Books', '0', 0, '9780124398603', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Lay, Thorne is the author of \\\'Structure and Fate of Subducting Slabs\\\', published 1996 under ISBN 9780124398603 and ISBN 012439860X.', '0.000000', 0.00, 83.39, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:53', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(57045, 'Value Management in Design and Construction The Economic Management of Projects', 'Kelly, John, Male, Steven', '', '', '1993', 'Routledge', '0', 0, '9780419151203', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Kelly, John is the author of \\\'Value Management in Design and Construction The Economic Management of Projects\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780419151203 and ISBN 0419151206.', '0.000000', 0.00, 59.46, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:53', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(57143, 'British Building Industry Since 1800 an Economic History', 'Powell, Christopher', '', '', '1996', 'Routledge', '0', 0, '9780419207306', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'This scholarly and well-researched study of the building industry documents the interplay of new materials and technologies, costs and the changing social and economic forces that affected the decision-making about our built environment over the last two centuries. The author provides a succinct and readable survey of the growth and development of British building which will be of interest to all building specialists and those training for a career in the construction industry.Powell, Christopher is the author of \\\'British Building Industry Since 1800 an Economic History\\\', published 1996 under ISBN 9780419207306 and ISBN 0419207309.', '0.000000', 0.00, 51.31, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:53', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(57160, 'Arbitration Practice in Construction Contracts', 'Stephenson, Douglas A.', '', '', '1993', 'Routledge', '0', 0, '9780419183303', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Considers each stage in the course of an arbitration in detail, from the claimant\\\'s decision to seek the means of resolving a dispute to the arbitrator\\\'s award, explaining clearly and concisely what is expected of the claimant, respondent and arbitrator and when.Stephenson, Douglas A. is the author of \\\'Arbitration Practice in Construction Contracts\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780419183303 and ISBN 0419183302.', '0.000000', 0.00, 128.32, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:54', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(57176, 'Information Management in a Contractor: A Model of the Flow of Project Data', 'Fisher, Norman, Yin, Shen L.', '', '', '1992', 'American Society of Civil Engineers', '0', 0, '9780727716668', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Fisher, Norman is the author of \\\'Information Management in a Contractor: A Model of the Flow of Project Data\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780727716668 and ISBN 0727716662.', '0.000000', 0.00, 110.69, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:54', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(57188, 'Inca Architecture and Construction at Ollantaytambo', 'Protzen, Jean-Pierre, Batson, Robert', '', '', '1993', 'Oxford University Press, Incorporated', '0', 0, '9780195070699', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'It is a modern-day mystery how the Inca, who did not have iron tools or knowledge of the wheel, mined and transported stones and dressed and fitted them in remarkable structures. Jean-Pierre Protzen has spent much of the past decade investigating the quarrying and stonecutting techniques of the Inca, and problems of Inca construction practices. His work is based principally on observation, careful measurements of structures, and experiments using stones and tools the Inca stonemasons would have used. Ollantaytambo, probably the best-preserved Inca town, offers an ideal laboratory with its well-thought-out site plans, its intimate integration of the built form with the natural environment, the unity of its architecture, and the sheer perfection of its cut-stone masonry. Offering the only extensive analysis of Inca construction practices, Protzen describes and interprets the archaeological complex of Ollantaytambo, discovers temporal and functional links among its components, uncovers the planning and design criteria that governed its layout and architecture, and compiles all that has been written about the site.Protzen, Jean-Pierre is the author of \\\'Inca Architecture and Construction at Ollantaytambo\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780195070699 and ISBN 0195070690.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:20:54', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
