(60339, 'Estimating for Residential Construction', 'Van Orman, H. A.', '', '', '1991', 'Delmar Cengage Learning', '0', 0, '9780827336445', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'The second edition of this highly practical book leads you step-by-step through all phases of estimating materials required in building a house. Emphasis is on how to make a material list for a house, how to place the list in workable order, and how to determine the cost for any particular job.Van Orman, H. A. is the author of \\\'Estimating for Residential Construction\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780827336445 and ISBN 0827336446.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:13', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(60342, 'Practical Problems in Mathematics for Carpenters', 'Huth, Harry C.', '', '', '1991', 'Delmar Cengage Learning', '0', 0, '9780827345805', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'The Practical Problems in Mathematics series offers students of specific trades useful help in basic mathematics and opportunities to practice math principles on problems applied to their area of interest. Practical Problems in Mathematics for Carpenters, seventh edition, contains 43 instructional units progressing from the simplest basic arithmetic operations to compound problems applied in light frame construction. Each of the 43 units begins with a brief review of the math principal to be applied in that unit. The book contains more than 800 carpentry problems, including two comprehensive tests.Huth, Harry C. is the author of \\\'Practical Problems in Mathematics for Carpenters\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780827345805 and ISBN 0827345801.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:13', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
