(62290, 'Home Wiring', 'Wood, Robert W.', '', '', '1992', 'McGraw-Hill Professional Publishing', '0', 0, '9780070717428', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Explains the basics of the home wiring system, covering all the most common electrical repairs. Detachable Tip Card provides a complete shopping list for basic repairs and installations.Wood, Robert W. is the author of \\\'Home Wiring\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780070717428 and ISBN 0070717427.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:26', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(62292, 'The Complete Guide of Home Inspection', 'Becher, Norman', '', '', '1992', 'McGraw-Hill Professional Publishing', '0', 0, '9780070045354', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Becher, Norman is the author of \\\'The Complete Guide of Home Inspection\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780070045354 and ISBN 0070045356.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:26', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(62295, 'Precision Casting Processes', 'Clegg, A. J.', '', '', '1991', 'Elsevier Science &amp; Technology Books', '0', 0, '9780080378794', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'The casting process is the most efficient and capable means of producing fully shaped components of any size, from most metals and alloys. Precision castings are renowned for their dimensional accuracy, consistency, improved surface finish and improved metallurgical integrity; all features which are increasingly demanded by casting users. Precision Casting Processes describes the principal casting production processes available to the foundry industry and reviews their ability to produce precision castings. With its main emphasis on the casting processes, the book also outlines casting design, metal melting and treatment, quality control procedures in the production of precision castings and examines quality control procedures used by the foundry industry. In covering all these topics, Precision Casting Processes provides a valuable information source for designers and users of castings, practising foundrymen, and students of engineering and materials.Clegg, A. J. is the author of \\\'Precision Casting Processes\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780080378794 and ISBN 008037879X.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:26', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(62330, 'Contract Administration for the Building Team', 'Aqua Group Staff, Bagnall, Brian', '', '', '1996', 'Wiley &amp; Sons, Incorporated, John', '0', 0, '9780632038473', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Aqua Group Staff is the author of \\\'Contract Administration for the Building Team\\\', published 1996 under ISBN 9780632038473 and ISBN 0632038470.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:26', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(62336, 'Pre-contract Studies: Development Economics, Tendering and Estimating (Chartered Institute o...', 'Ashworth, Allan', '', '', '1996', 'Addison-Wesley Longman, Incorporated', '0', 0, '9780582249844', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Pre-contract Studies: Development Economics and Estimating provides a comprehensive introduction to the property development process. It covers the level 2 module of the CIOB\\\'s Education Framework on pre-contract studies and is officially sanctioned by the CIOB as the recognised text for that module. The book addresses the issues involved in development with an emphasis on the financial analysis of projects in the context of development values and construction costs. The process of getting a project from inception to completion is thoroughly examined, while the different methods of development appraisal and the way that developers\\\' budgets are calculated are further explored through worked examples. This book is a core textbook for the CIOB level 2 module on pre-contract studies, as well as BTEC HNC/D and degree courses in building and surveying. It is also useful reading for degree courses in estate management and architecture.Ashworth, Allan is the author of \\\'Pre-contract Studies: Development Economics, Tendering and Estimating (Chartered Institute of Building)\\\', published 1996 under ISBN 9780582249844 and ISBN 0582249848.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:26', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(62376, 'How to Contract the Building of Your New Home', 'Shepherd, James M., Wilson, Andrew, Dreiling, H.', '', '', '1991', 'Shepherd Publishers', '0', 0, '9780960730872', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'Completely covers all of the tasks the general contractor must do in terms the layman can easily understand & do himself. Home-owners-to-be can save up to twenty percent of the cost of the building their new home with the work be done by professional subcontractors. As G.T. of Houston said, \\\"Your book is superb. Absolutely no library book nor general information is available that covers all aspects of building as yours does.\\\"Shepherd, James M. is the author of \\\'How to Contract the Building of Your New Home\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780960730872 and ISBN 0960730877.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:26', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(62387, 'Underground Structures - Design and Construction', 'Sinha, R. S.', '', '', '1991', 'Elsevier Science &amp; Technology Books', '0', 0, '9780444889911', '', 'C002; C011; C015; C026; C035; C036', 'This volume presents the most up-to-date information collected on the design and construction of underground structures - tunnels, shafts and chambers. There is extensive discussion on the design of rock and soil tunnels, subsurface investigation, laboratory and (in situ) tests on host ground, drilling and blasting, tunnel-boring and other machines, freezing, grouting, construction methods, lake tap and cost estimating. Civil, structural, geotechnical and planning aspects for the design and construction of underground structures are covered in detail. This book and its complimentary volume \\\"Underground Structures - Design and Instrumentation\\\", together should serve the engineering and construction needs of planners, executives, geologists, civil-, structural-, and geotechnical engineers, who are interested in the design, construction and operation of underground structures.Sinha, R. S. is the author of \\\'Underground Structures - Design and Construction\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780444889911 and ISBN 0444889914.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:21:26', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
