(69470, 'Handbook of Electrical and Electronic Insulating Materials', 'Shugg, W. Tillar', '', '', '1995', 'Wiley &amp; Sons, Incorporated, John', '0', 0, '9780780310308', '', 'C043; C044; C045; C046; C076', 'Electrical Engineering/Power and Energy Handbook of Electrical and Electronic Insulating Materials, Second Edition \\\"This edition preserves the best of the original and updates the text admirably.\\\" -Ron Sampson, Consultant, Technology Seminars, Inc. The only single source devoted to all classes of insulating materials for electrical and electronic applications, this definitive handbook offers immediate and easy access to detailed information in one easy-to-use source. Each product classification includes: Major producers Technologies and methods of manufacture Trade names Applicable standards and specifications Properties and uses Development programs and market trends You will also find information on SI symbols and their applications, conversion factors for frequently used units, and an extensive temperature conversion chart -a wealth of data that is free of excessive technical jargon. This book will be invaluable to electrical and electronics engineers who need to make informed choices about dielectric and electrical insulation materials as well as technologists in related fields who need a comprehensive reference. Also of Interest From IEEE Press... Metric Units and Conversion Charts A Metrication Handbook for Engineers, Technologists, and Scientists, Second Edition by Theodore Wildi, Sperika Enterprises, Ltd., Canada 1995 / Softcover / 144 pp / ISBN 0-7803-1050-0 / IEEE Order No. PP4044 Analysis of Electric Machinery by Paul C. Krause and Oleg Wasynczuk, Purdue University and Scott D. Sudhoff, University of Missouri at Rolla 1994 / Hardcover / 584 pp / ISBN 0-7803-1101-9 / IEEE Order No. PC4556Shugg, W. Tillar is the author of \\\'Handbook of Electrical and Electronic Insulating Materials\\\', published 1995 under ISBN 9780780310308 and ISBN 0780310306.', '0.000000', 0.00, 91.76, '', '', '2024-10-19 17:29:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
