(77998, 'METALLIZATION: THEORY & PRACTICE VLSI', 'Murarka, Shyam P.', '', '', '1992', 'Elsevier Science &amp; Technology Books', '0', 0, '9780750690010', '', 'C047; C048; C049; C077; C135; C148', 'This title covers fundemental concepts, properties and applicabilities of metals and alloys for use in various metallization schemes. Metallizations form the key components on electronic circuits - controlling device properties and providing power and device interconnections with the outside world or with other devices. The recent advent of submicron dimensions and increasingly faster devices in the semiconductor have challenged researchers to keep metallization schemes in line with new demanding requirements.Murarka, Shyam P. is the author of \\\'METALLIZATION: THEORY & PRACTICE VLSI\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780750690010 and ISBN 0750690011.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 20:49:55', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
