(90168, 'Combustion and Pollution Control in Heating Systems', 'Hanby, V.I.', '', '', '1994', 'Springer', '0', 0, '9783540198499', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', 'The combustion of hydrocarbon fuels in heating systems is an important topic for students taking courses in building services and related areas including mechanical engineering. The control of pollution from this source is of increasing importance to planners, architects, builders, commercial and industrial property owners and legislators.Combustion and Pollution Control in Heating Systems provides a comprehensive coverage of this environmentally sensitive topic for the first time. The fundamental principles of the combustion process are explained. Special attention is given to the processes which take place in boilers. The author has extensive experience in teaching this subject at the Universities at Loughborough and Liverpool.Hanby, V.I. is the author of \\\'Combustion and Pollution Control in Heating Systems\\\', published 1994 under ISBN 9783540198499 and ISBN 3540198490.', '0.000000', 0.00, 51.31, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:57:45', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
