(91437, 'Toilet Papers: Recycling Waste and Conserving Water', 'Van der Ryn, Sim', '', '', '1995', 'Ecological Design Press', '0', 0, '9780964471801', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', 'A classic is back in print! One of the favorite books of 1970s back-to-the-landers, The Toilet Papers is an informative, inspiring, and irreverent look at how people have dealt with their wastes through the centuries. In a historical survey, Van der Ryn provides the basic facts concerning human wastes, and describes safe designs for toilets that reduce water consumption and avert the necessity for expensive and unreliable treatment systems. The Toilet Papers provides do-it-yourself plans for a basic compost privy and a variety of graywater systems.Van der Ryn, Sim is the author of \\\'Toilet Papers: Recycling Waste and Conserving Water\\\', published 1995 under ISBN 9780964471801 and ISBN 0964471809.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:57:56', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
