(97156, 'Water Quality Management Library Toxicity Reduction  Evaluation and Control', 'Ford, Davis L.', '', '', '1992', 'C R C Press LLC', '0', 0, '9780877629054', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', 'In the reauthorization of the Clean Water Act in 1987, the U.S. EPA specifically addressed toxics management. In addition to the requirement to eliminate discharge of toxics, there can be a requirement to conduct a toxicity reduction evaluation (TRE). The scope of toxicity reduction varies from the very simple and inexpensive to the highly complex and costly. This book, volume three of the Water Quality Management Library, provides a complete overview of toxicity reduction evaluation. The book presents the testing and removal of toxicants, toxicity testing procedures, sampling techniques, baseline collection data, and source identification. Plus, the book presents toxicity reduction methodologies including unit processes necessary for organic toxicant control using biological and physical chemical methodologies as well as selected unit processes necessary for inorganic toxicant control.Ford, Davis L. is the author of \\\'Water Quality Management Library Toxicity Reduction  Evaluation and Control\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9780877629054 and ISBN 0877629056.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:58:47', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(97157, 'Water Quality Modeling Decision Support Techniques for Lakes and Reservoirs', 'Henderson-Sellers, Brian', '', '', '1991', 'C R C Press LLC', '0', 0, '9780849369742', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', 'This volume represents the first decision support book aimed at water quality management for lakes and reservoirs. The book offers both a retrospective view (in terms of summarizing past work) and a prospective view (in terms of forecasting the greater use of such models as part of much needed environmental decision support systems). The concepts of lake and reservoir simulation modeling, as well as the concepts of decision support systems, formalized within the information systems discipline, are supported by a wealth of case studies. Case studies in the early chapters concentrate more on the physical (dynamic and thermodynamic) parameters, while later chapters stress the need for a more detailed representation of the biology and chemistry. Other case studies emphasize the management use of the model. New tools and concepts are also presented to facilitate the transfer of case studies presented in this volume from the arena of research to that of operational and planning management. Water quality managers,research scientists, and water engineers will find this volume an exciting source of new ideas and concepts.Henderson-Sellers, Brian is the author of \\\'Water Quality Modeling Decision Support Techniques for Lakes and Reservoirs\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780849369742 and ISBN 0849369746.', '0.000000', 0.00, 286.46, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:58:47', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(97159, 'Water Quality Modeling Applications to Estuaries', 'Lung, Wu-Seng, French', '', '', '1993', 'C R C Press LLC', '0', 0, '9780849369735', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', 'This volume to discussing the various aspects of estuarine water quality modeling. Topics considered include fundamental principles, estuarine mass transport, BOD/DO and eutrophication model kinetics, kinetics on toxicants, and sediment-water interactions. The book also discusses mixing zone modeling and how to integrate estuarine hydrodynamic and water quality models. Many case studies demonstrating successful model applications are discussed.Lung, Wu-Seng is the author of \\\'Water Quality Modeling Applications to Estuaries\\\', published 1993 under ISBN 9780849369735 and ISBN 0849369738.', '0.000000', 0.00, 216.80, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:58:47', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(97160, 'Water Quality Modelling', 'Falconer, Roger A.', '', '', '1992', 'Ashgate Publishing, Limited', '0', 0, '9781857420340', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', 'Falconer, Roger A. is the author of \\\'Water Quality Modelling\\\', published 1992 under ISBN 9781857420340 and ISBN 1857420349.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:58:47', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(97193, 'Water Quality Control at Shiplocks Prevention of Salt- And Fresh Water Exchange', 'Kerstma, J., Kolkman, P. A., Regeling, H. J.', '', '', '1994', 'Taylor &amp; Francis Group', '0', 0, '9789054101420', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', 'An overview of research on the separation of salt and fresh water at ship locks in the Netherlands. The text aims to provide deeper insights that could prove beneficial for future projects. Where possible, results of research with scale models, theory and real life experience are noted.Kerstma, J. is the author of \\\'Water Quality Control at Shiplocks Prevention of Salt- And Fresh Water Exchange\\\', published 1994 under ISBN 9789054101420 and ISBN 9054101423.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:58:47', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
