(97265, 'Troubled Waters Champion International and the Pigeon River Controversy', 'Bartlett, Richard A.', '', '', '1995', 'University of Tennessee Press', '0', 0, '9780870498879', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', '\\\"A thoroughly documented and well-written, important case study in environmental history.\\\"Bartlett, Richard A. is the author of \\\'Troubled Waters Champion International and the Pigeon River Controversy\\\', published 1995 under ISBN 9780870498879 and ISBN 0870498878.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:58:48', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
(97268, 'Underground Storage Tank Management A Practical Guide', 'Rizzo, Joyce A.', '', '', '1991', 'Government Institutes', '0', 0, '9780865872714', '', 'C054; C055; C056; C057; C058; C079; C080', 'The Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) is requiring that all UST owners & operators comply with new federal requirements by December 22, 1998. As a result, the federal regulatory program for underground storage tanks (UST) has spirited considerable activity in the development of regulatory programs & new technology for compliance. The new Underground Storage Tank Management, 5th Edition, includes updates in requirements & technology & addresses the extensive changes made to UST management in the last six years. This practical guide to regulatory compliance & good management practice addresses key issues in UST management. Author Joyce A. Rizzo offers recommendations for developing & maintaining UST management programs that not only minimize the risk of a release but also reduce the potential for costly repercussions. This 5th Edition contains five new chapters that address updates to the U.S. EPA\\\'s approval of state regulatory & trust fund programs, soil sampling & analytical guidelines, the evolution of tank testing strategies, National Fire Protection Pamphlet 329, new state-of-the-art technology, & SPCC plans.Rizzo, Joyce A. is the author of \\\'Underground Storage Tank Management A Practical Guide\\\', published 1991 under ISBN 9780865872714 and ISBN 0865872716.', '0.000000', 0.00, 0.00, '', '', '2024-10-19 21:58:48', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 0, 0, 0, 0),
