(275056, '2591916', 'TIA TIA/EIA-136-410-1', 'TDMA- Cellular PCS-Radio Interface-Enhanced Full-Rate Voice Codec Addendum 1', 'Revised', '', '', '', '', NULL, 'TIA - Telecommunications Industry Association', 'English', 'REAFFIRMED 08/14/2013', '', '100.00', '', 'USD', '', '', '', '', '', '2001', '18', '', '', '', '', ''),
(275057, '2593816', 'TIA ANSI/TIA/EIA-136-410-1', 'TDMA Cellular PCS - Radio Interface - Enhanced Full-Rate Voice Codec', 'Revised', '', '', '', '', NULL, 'TIA - Telecommunications Industry Association', 'English', 'TIA/EIA-136-410\n        \n\n      Preface\r\nThis document gives a description of the ACELP speech and\r\nchannel codec for a TIA Enhanced Full Rate Codec. The codec\r\nconsists of a 7.4 kb/s ACELP speech codec and two channel codecs\r\n(Forward Error Correction): a 5.6 kb/s channel codec and a 6.5 kb/s\r\nchannel codec.\r\nSection 1 gives a general description of the speech coder and\r\nsections 2 and 3 give more detailed descriptions of the speech\r\nencoder and the speech decoder, respectively. Section 4 gives a\r\ndetailed description of the two channel encoders. The channel\r\ndecoder in section 5 is not considered as part of this standard.\r\nThe bad frame masking described in section 5.1 is provided as an\r\nexample solution; other solutions are allowed. Section 6 gives a\r\ndetailed description of the different aspects of Discontinuous\r\nTransmission (DTX). The bad frame masking described in section\r\n6.4.4 is provided as an example solution; other solutions are\r\nallowed.\r\nThis standard consists of this document and a soft copy\r\ndistribution on a CD ROM. These I contain a bit-exact description\r\nin the form of a fixed point ANSI C code and a number of test\r\nsequences. The C code defies the speech codec and the channel\r\nencoder with a set of fixed point basic operators. The test vectors\r\nare described in Annex A. A detailed description of the contents\r\nand formats of the soft copy distribution is given in Annex B. The\r\ndetails of the instability protection for the speech codec are\r\ngiven in Annex C. Annex D describes a reference design of a voice\r\nactivity detector WAD) which may be used to implement the DTX mode\r\nof the speech encoder in the mobile station (MS).\r\nMS implementations shall be bit-exact. Bit-exact implementations\r\nare subject to the test vectors specified in this standard. Base\r\nstation implementations are not required to be bit-exact. However,\r\nnon bit-exact validation is subject to the minimum performance\r\nrequirements for the Enhanced Full Rate codec contained in TIMEIA\r\nIS-686-A.\r\nIn the case of discrepancy between the high level and the\r\nbit-exact descriptions, the description in the bit-exact C program\r\nwill prevail.', '', '100.00', '', 'USD', 'TIA TIA-136-410;TIA ANSI/TIA/EIA-136-410', '2593838;2592751', '', '', '', '2001', '16', '', '', '', '', ''),
